From aa616745438c7a0eda71255102b0ad2cc457f1b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:07:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] samba: /var/lib/samba/private is 0700 on every start

The five runtime directories v3.4.0 moved ahead of enrollment come from
mkdir_if_none, which makes them 0777; Samba installs private as 0700
(secrets.tdb, the messaging sockets) and never re-checks it. chmod after
the mkdirs; /var is tmpfs, so nothing of a user's is touched. Lean:
tests/test_samba_enroll_dirs.py; REAPER-FIXES C18.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 release/src/router/rc/usb.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/usb.c b/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
index d9c1768487..347bb7e0ee 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/usb.c
@@ -3624,6 +3624,10 @@ start_samba(void)
 	mkdir_if_none("/var/lib/samba");
 	mkdir_if_none("/var/lib/samba/private");
 	mkdir_if_none("/var/cache/samba");
+	/* reaper 2026-10-13: mkdir_if_none makes 0777 directories; Samba installs private
+	   0700 (secrets.tdb, the messaging sockets) and never re-checks it, so hold it there
+	   on every start. /var is tmpfs: nothing of a user's is touched. */
+	chmod("/var/lib/samba/private", 0700);
 #endif
 
 	unlink("/etc/smb.conf");
-- 
